🌒Laura Palmer? or Marilyn Monroe?
the-woman-in-trouble dream

порой хочется облокотиться на спинку кресла, закинуть ногу на ногу и с кинопоисковским шармом начать: “А знаете ли вы что?...” 

…that Laura Palmer is actually a blonde protagonist who mirrors Marilyn Monroe?💔

🍪Originally David Lynch was going to make a film based on the diaries of Monroe and her mysterious death (which he believed was murder), but the studio dropped the film and the Monroe’s movie idea became inspiration for a mind-bending TV show Twin Peaks.

so, what does ill-fated homecoming queen Laura Palmer have in common with the enigmatic Marilyn Monroe?

🔘both are blonde women who died tragically at a young age and inspired a state of mourning locally (Laura) and globally (Marilyn);
🔘there were several conspiracy theories surrounding Monroe’s death in a similar manner to how Palmer’s death was investigated in the show;
🔘for both of them drug addiction was a way to cope with stress: Palmer was heavily addicted to cocaine due to her mental problems, Marilyn was open about her struggles with mental health and addiction to prescription drugs;
🔘Monroe secretly made tape recordings for her psychiatrist in the days before she died, just like Laura recorded her innermost thoughts and sent the tapes to Dr.Jacoby;
🔘Laura Palmer was sexually abused by 🤫her dad for years; Marilyn Monroe suffered sexual abuse at the hands of one of her caretakers when she was a child.

🧿 однако для Линча история о Лоре/Мэрилин была не только о личной трагедии потерявшихся женщин, Линч также стремился разрушить идею идеальности той самой American dream, приоткрывая завесу ужаса и боли, скрытых за нашими идеалистичными фантазиями.

➖➖➖➖➖
Glossary

💋 mind-bending = having a strong effect on your mind; галлюциногенный; 
💋 ill-fated = unlucky and unsuccessful, often resulting in death; 
💋 homecoming queen = королева бала; 
💋 enigmatic = mysterious, impossible to understand completely; 
💋 mourning = скорбь; 
💋 innermost = most secret & hidden.

